From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netifd: refresh the main device during hotplug replacement

A wireless interface can move between radios before its previous device
is removed. Releasing the hotplug main device invalidates the cached master
pointer. Refresh it before testing bridge operations so the retired
non-bridge device cannot reject its successor.

Preserve configured masters and checks against removing a different device.
This device-owner correction does not depend on wireless bridge-forwarding
policy.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

--- a/interface.c
+++ b/interface.c
@@ -1285,8 +1285,10 @@ interface_add_link(struct interface *ifa
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	if (iface->main_dev.hotplug)
+	if (iface->main_dev.hotplug) {
 		interface_set_main_dev(iface, NULL);
+		mdev = iface->main_dev.dev;
+	}
 
 	if (mdev) {
 		if (mdev->hotplug_ops)
